  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For a North America hotel positioned around **differentiated guest experience** and **local character**, the strongest lifestyle brands to consider are **Kimpton**, **Hotel Indigo**, **Canopy by Hilton**, **Graduate**, **Moxy**, **W Hotels**, **Autograph Collection**, **Curio Collection**, **Tapestry Collection**, and **Hyatt’s Unbound Collection / Destination Hotels**.[7][11][16][17]\n\nThese brands are repeatedly described as emphasizing **design-led**, **locally inspired**, and **experience-driven** stays:\n- **Kimpton, Hotel Indigo, and voco** are explicitly positioned by IHG as “design-led, locally inspired” with a boutique feel.[7]\n- **Canopy by Hilton** is framed around local energy and culture, while **Graduate** leans into local history, charm, and pop-culture identity.[11]\n- **W Hotels** is described by Marriott as an iconic luxury lifestyle brand with compelling design, unexpected experiences, and highly activated spaces.[2]\n- **Autograph Collection**, **Curio Collection**, and **Tapestry Collection** are commonly cited as soft-brand/lifestyle options for owners seeking local character with larger-system distribution and loyalty reach.[5][17]\n- **Hyatt’s Unbound Collection** and **Destination Hotels** are also positioned in the lifestyle/soft-brand space with a local-story angle.[17]\n\nIf you want the most “local character first” shortlist, I’d prioritize:\n- **Hotel Indigo**\n- **Kimpton**\n- **Canopy by Hilton**\n- **Graduate**\n- **Autograph Collection**\n- **Curio Collection**\n- **Tapestry Collection**\n- **Unbound Collection**\n- **Destination Hotels**[7][11][17]\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into a **brand-by-brand owner fit matrix** for North America by segment, conversion potential, and required capital.",
